---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AboutCard from './components/Card';
import Grid from './components/Grid';
---

<Layout
  title="About | Jacob Chesslo"
  description="About Jacob Chesslo - software engineer, physicist, Eagle Scout, and community leader."
>
  <main class="py-12">
    <!-- Hero Header -->
    <div class="text-center mb-12">
      <h1
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-[#f0ece4] mb-3"
        style="font-family: 'Syne', sans-serif; text-shadow: 2px 2px 0 rgba(139,92,246,0.5);"
      >
        Jacob Chesslo
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[#a78bfa] italic text-sm tracking-wide" style="font-family: var(--font-mono);">
        they/them/theirs • he/him/his
      </p>
      <div
        class="w-24 h-1 mx-auto bg-gradient-to-r from-[#8b5cf6] via-[#7c3aed] to-[#a78bfa] rounded-full mt-4"
      >
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Education Section -->
    <Grid title="My Love of Education">
      <AboutCard client:load title="Albert Gallatin Area School District">
        High School Diploma, class of 2017. Graduated Summa Cum Laude with a 4.5 GPA and was
        selected as Graduation Speaker. Active in AP coursework, National Honor Society, drumline,
        debate team, and the Young Astronauts Club.
      </AboutCard>
      <AboutCard client:load title="Florida Institute of Technology">
        B.S. Physics with a Minor in Chemistry, graduated Cum Laude (GPA 3.48) in December 2020.
        Coursework spanned quantum mechanics, electromagnetism, subatomic physics, thermodynamics,
        and computational methods. Involved in SPS, SEDS, the Student Rocket Society, and the
        Student Government Association.
      </AboutCard>
      <AboutCard client:load title="Continuing">
        Began an M.S. in Computer Science at the University of Central Florida (4.0 GPA) with a
        focus on Quantum Computing before transitioning to industry. Ongoing self-study in high
        energy physics, cosmology, AI/ML, and quantum information theory.
      </AboutCard>
    </Grid>

    <!-- Experience Section -->
    <Grid title="My Love to Make a Difference">
      <AboutCard client:load title="Eagle Scout">
        Earned the rank of Eagle Scout in December 2016 - the highest rank in Boy Scouts of America.
        Also inducted into the Order of the Arrow. Scouting instilled a commitment to service,
        leadership, and leaving things better than I found them.
      </AboutCard>
      <AboutCard client:load title="Research Assistant in High Energy Particle Physics">
        Worked with the Hohlmann Research Group at Florida Tech from 2018–2020, contributing to two
        CMS/CERN projects: a vector-portal dark matter search using MadGraph and PYTHIA8, and the
        design and construction of a modular Gas Electron Multiplier (GEM) detector for the future
        Electron-Ion Collider. Results presented at the FIT Student Design Showcase.
      </AboutCard>
      <AboutCard client:load title="Pi Lambda Phi">
        Served in five consecutive leadership roles in the Florida Delta Upsilon Chapter -
        Treasurer, VP of Education, President, Social Media Director, and New Member Educator -
        before becoming President and then Board of Trustee of the Alumni Association. Recipient of
        the Fraternity Man of the Year award (2021) from Florida Tech's Office of Fraternity and
        Sorority Life.
      </AboutCard>
    </Grid>
  </main>
</Layout>
